Defects found:

- Line 32: `run("probe.py", cwd=<tmp containing tmp/scripts/probe.py>)` executes `REPO/scripts/probe.py`, not `<tmp>/scripts/probe.py`. Consequence: the harness can test a different script copy than the one it just staged.

- Lines 61-75: input `scripts/baselines/x_self_describing.json` containing `{"claims":["a","b"]}`. Consequence: this graft writes the real worktree baseline, contradicting “copy in a temp directory” and risking corpus mutation.

- Lines 66 and 77: input baseline bytes `{\r\n "claims": ["a"]\r\n}\r\n`. Consequence: restore reads universal newlines and writes LF, so unchanged logical content becomes a changed file.

- Line 69: input baseline JSON `{"notes":["not a claim"],"claims":["a","b"]}`. Consequence: the first non-empty list is shrunk, so the probe may not remove a safety claim at all.

- Lines 95-97: input `arni-hfref.json` with `{"manuscript":{"body":"x"*201},"screening":{"duplicate_screening":{"performed_by_two":true}}}`. Consequence: the graft claims to name a field the object does not hold, but no absence check exists, so the constructed input may not be failing.

- Lines 135-136: input result tuple `("x", 2, "graft", "python: can't open file")`. Consequence: any subprocess crash or missing script is reported as “CAN FIRE, CONDITION ABSENT.”

